==English==

===Etymology===
{{confix|en|a|biblio-|phobia}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|humorous}} Fear of running out of things to [[read]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|title=The Jewish Quarterly|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=D8JVAAAAYAAJ&q=%22abibliophobia%22&dq=%22abibliophobia%22|page=72
|passage=Professor David Latchman, the Master of Birkbeck College, suffers from '''''abibliophobia''''', a common affliction amongst book collectors that manifests itself as a morbid fear of running out of reading material.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Phil Cousineau|title=Wordcatcher: An Odyssey into the World of Weird and Wonderful Words|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=LpPGAgAAQBAJ&pg=PT39&dq=%22abibliophobia%22|page=17|publisher=Viva Editions|isbn=9781573444002
